# C1 step 5: modules/scanning/README.md documents the module.
# Names must appear as the first cell of a table row (| name |), not just anywhere.
modules/scanning/README.md | ^# [A-Za-z] | must start with a title: a line beginning with one # and a name (## is a subheading, not a title)
modules/scanning/README.md | ^##+ .*Requirements | needs a "Requirements" section
modules/scanning/README.md | ^##+ .*Usage | needs a "Usage" section
modules/scanning/README.md | ^##+ .*Inputs | needs an "Inputs" section
modules/scanning/README.md | ^##+ .*Outputs | needs an "Outputs" section
modules/scanning/README.md | ^\| *`?terraform`? *\| | needs a Requirements row for terraform
modules/scanning/README.md | ^\| *`?aws`? *\| | needs a Requirements row for the aws provider
modules/scanning/README.md | module "scanning" | the Usage block must show module "scanning"
modules/scanning/README.md | source *= *"\./modules/scanning" | the Usage block must set source = "./modules/scanning"
modules/scanning/README.md | ^[A-Z][^|]{25,}\.$ | needs a one-sentence description: a line of text that starts with a capital letter and ends with a period
modules/scanning/README.md | ^\| *`?project_name`? *\| | needs a table row for the project_name input
modules/scanning/README.md | ^\| *`?incoming_bucket_name`? *\| | needs a table row for the incoming_bucket_name input
modules/scanning/README.md | ^\| *`?incoming_bucket_arn`? *\| | needs a table row for the incoming_bucket_arn input
modules/scanning/README.md | ^\| *`?router_lambda_arn`? *\| | needs a table row for the router_lambda_arn input
modules/scanning/README.md | ^\| *`?alert_email`? *\| | needs a table row for the alert_email input
modules/scanning/README.md | ^\| *`?guardduty_role_arn`? *\| | needs a table row for the guardduty_role_arn output
modules/scanning/README.md | ^\| *`?guardduty_plan_id`? *\| | needs a table row for the guardduty_plan_id output
